<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ogaden</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ogaden plateau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ogaden is a plateau and lowland region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a>, today forming part of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. Its pastoral hinterland supplied livestock for export and recruits for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>'s armies, drawn largely from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> nomads. The sultanate governed a confederation of pastoral and commercial communities across the Ogaden and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ogaden.jpg" alt="Ogaden" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States. Central Intelligence Agency · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethiopia,_the_Ogaden_Region._LOC_91682434.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
